#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD9714 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "FOUR rows, ONE finding. LBORRES carries at least one non-empty value but the LBORRESU column is not present at all. Since the D-6 hoist (2026-09-12) the absence half lives in Requirements.Variables.None [--ORRESU] - satisfied here, the column is absent - and the Check is the single broadcast leaf not var_is_empty(--ORRES), false-on-nothing here because a value exists, so the verdict is ONE per dataset. MULTI-ROW ON PURPOSE (2026-09-11): the fixture was a single row, so it passed identically whether the rule routed per dataset or per record and the corpus could not see the flood -- this rule was minted by Fix #330 to REPLACE a per-record flood, and until var_is_empty was registered as a broadcast column predicate it emitted 4 findings here, one of them naming the row whose LBORRES is empty. Row 3 is deliberately empty for that reason. The sibling SD0026 cannot see this: it needs --ORRESU in Requirements.Variables.All and therefore SKIPs."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 40
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALT | 22
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1023 | 1 | ALB |
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1023 | 2 | ALT | 31
